      "source": [
        "# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Initial Procedures\n",
        "\n",
        "### Importing Data\n",
        "In this section, necessary Python libraries are imported, and the dataset containing all of the elements is read into the environment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Import necessary libraries\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# Read the dataset\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv('datasheet.csv')\n",
        "# Delete all empty columns\n",
        "df = df.loc[:, ~df.columns.str.contains('^Unnamed')]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Cleaning and Organizing Data\n",
        "\n",
        "In this section, we reorganized and cleanted the dataset by deleting empty columns on the csv file, renaming columns for clarity, and converting some data to numeric to manipulate and work on the data easily.\n\n",
        "The organized dataset contains 'DATE', 'TotalSleep_min', 'REM_min', 'Light_min', 'Deep_min', 'Caffeine_mg', and 'Productivity_min' information, where min indicates minutes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Rename columns for clarity\n",
        "df.columns = [\n",
        "    'DATE', 'TotalSleep', 'TotalSleep_min', 'REM', 'REM_min',\n",
        "    'Light', 'Light_min', 'Deep', 'Deep_min', 'Caffeine_mg',\n",
        "    'Productivity', 'Productivity_min'\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert Caffeine to numeric\n",
        "df['Caffeine_mg'] = df['Caffeine_mg'].str.replace('mg','').str.strip()\n",
        "df['Caffeine_mg'] = pd.to_numeric(df['Caffeine_mg'], errors='coerce')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert DATE to datetime format and sort\n",
        "df['DATE'] = pd.to_datetime(df['DATE'] + ' 2025', format='%B %d %Y', errors='coerce')\n",
        "df.sort_values('DATE', inplace=True)\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Dataset Overview and Summary Statistics \n",
        "\n",
        "In this part, we compute the main statistical measures for our variables including count, mean, standard deviation and min/max values with the code beneath. "
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "                  count    mean         std    min    25%    50%    75%    max\n",
            "Caffeine_mg        25.0  114.76  113.518457    0.0   25.0  135.0  135.0  410.0\n",
            "Productivity_min   25.0  196.60  100.485488   60.0  105.0  180.0  300.0  360.0\n",
            "TotalSleep_min     25.0  438.60   52.605450  324.0  412.0  450.0  468.0  557.0\n",
            "REM_min            25.0   95.28   23.129202   49.0   85.0   95.0  107.0  145.0\n",
            "Light_min          25.0  288.68   42.891064  191.0  271.0  290.0  317.0  379.0\n",
            "Deep_min           25.0   51.56   12.662543   33.0   39.0   52.0   59.0   75.0\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
        "source": [
            "\n",
            "# Printing the summary statistics\n",
            "stats = df[['Caffeine_mg', 'Productivity_min', 'TotalSleep_min',\n",
            "            'REM_min', 'Light_min', 'Deep_min']].describe().T \n",
            "print(stats)",
            "\n"
          ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "**Findings from the Summary Statistics**\n",
        "\n",
        "- The average daily caffeine intake is approximately 115 mg, with a standard deviation of 114 mg, indicating high variability. Some days had very little caffeine intake, while on other days it exceeded 400 mg.\n", 
        "- Total sleep time is fairly consistent, averaging 439 minutes (approximately 7.3 hours) with a standard deviation of 53 minutes.\n",
        "- Sleep quality statistics:\n",
        "  - REM sleep averages 95 minutes, with moderate variability.\n",
        "  - Light sleep is the largest portion of sleep, averaging 289 minutes, with some days significantly higher or lower.\n",
        "  - Deep sleep averages 52 minutes, being the most stable sleep stage with lower variability.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, sleep times are relatively stable, whereas caffeine intake and productivity show wider fluctuations, suggesting that there could be a stronger correlation between caffeine consumption and productivity.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Correlation Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "This section investigates the relationships between daily caffeine consumption, total sleep duration, different sleep stages (indicating sleep quality), and productivity. A correlation matrix was computed for six variables: Caffeine_mg, TotalSleep_min, REM_min, Light_min, Deep_min, and Productivity_min. \n",
        "\n",
        "Main Insights from the Heatmap:\n",
        "- `Productivity_min` is strongly positively correlated with `Caffeine_mg`\n",
        "- `Productivity_min` has a moderate positive correlation with each of `TotalSleep_min`, `REM_min`, and `Light_min`.\n",
        "- Surprisingly, a weak negative correlation exists between `Deep_min` and `Productivity_min`.\n",
        "\n",
        "This analysis gives us a solid starting point to investigate and test hypotheses about how sleep and caffeine influence productivity.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": null,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
          "# CORRELATION MATRIX\n",
          "all_corr = df[['TotalSleep_min', 'REM_min', 'Light_min', 'Deep_min', 'Caffeine_mg', 'Productivity_min']].corr()\n",
          "print(\"Correlation Matrix for All Variables:\\n\", all_corr)\n",
          "plt.figure(figsize=(8,6))\n",
          "sns.heatmap(all_corr, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', fmt=\".2f\")\n",
          "plt.title('Correlation Matrix: Sleep, Caffeine & Productivity')\n",
          "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "![Correlation Matrix](figures/correlationmatrix.jpg)\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Visualization\n",
        "\n",
        "###Daily Caffeine Intake Distribution\n",
        "This histogram shows the distribution of daily caffeine consumption throughout the observation period, which is about a month.\n",
        "\n",
        "The frequency of values indicates that caffeine intake was irregular. Most days fall within a lower to moderate consumption range, while a few days show remarkably high intake. The distribution is skewed to the right, meaning that lower caffeine consumption was more frequent, although there were occasional high values. The irregular peaks might reflect days with higher workload, such as exam periods, which could later help us explain the observed patterns of productivity.\n",
        "\n",
      ]
    },
